From: Priyansh Jain <priyansh.jain@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: Add SoC power-limit based thermal control for Qualcomm Kalambo

Origin: not yet
Forwarded: not yet
Applied-Upstream: not yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-12

Add a power-limit based thermal configuration for the Qualcomm Kalambo
CRD platform:

- Monitor the EC thermal sensor (ec-back-cover).
- Drive the SPEL SoC PL1 power-capping cooling device
  (spel_controller_soc_pl1) via its powercap sysfs interface.
- Use an incremental PID controller to adjust the power limit.
- Declare the platform's supported power and time-window range via
  PPCC so thermald can validate requested limits.

Signed-off-by: Priyansh Jain <priyansh.jain@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
Index: pkg-thermald/data/thermal-conf.xml
===================================================================
--- pkg-thermald.orig/data/thermal-conf.xml
+++ pkg-thermald/data/thermal-conf.xml
@@ -256,5 +256,57 @@ use "man thermal-conf.xml" for details
 		</CoolingDevice>
 	</CoolingDevices>
 </Platform>
+<!-- Thermal configuration example for Qualcomm platforms using SoCModel.
+     SoCModel is matched as a prefix against /sys/firmware/devicetree/base/model.
+     e.g. "Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. Kalambo CRD" will match
+          SoCModel "Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. Kalambo"
+-->
+<Platform>
+	<Name>Qualcomm Kalambo Platform</Name>
+	<SoCModel>Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. Kalambo CRD</SoCModel>
+	<PollingInterval>5</PollingInterval>
+	<PPCC>
+		<PowerLimitMinimum>10000</PowerLimitMinimum> <!-- 10W minimum -->
+		<PowerLimitMaximum>38000</PowerLimitMaximum> <!-- 38W maximum -->
+		<TimeWindowMinimum>15000</TimeWindowMinimum> <!-- 15 second minimum -->
+		<TimeWindowMaximum>630000</TimeWindowMaximum> <!-- 630 second maximum -->
+	</PPCC>
+	<ThermalSensors>
+		<ThermalSensor>
+			<Type>ec-back-cover</Type>
+			<AsyncCapable>0</AsyncCapable>
+		</ThermalSensor>
+	</ThermalSensors>
+	<ThermalZones>
+		<ThermalZone>
+			<Type>ec-back-cover</Type>
+			<TripPoints>
+				<TripPoint>
+					<SensorType>ec-back-cover</SensorType>
+					<Temperature>48000</Temperature> <!-- 48C -->
+					<Hyst>2000</Hyst>
+					<type>passive</type>
+					<CoolingDevice>
+						<Type>spel_controller_soc_pl1</Type>
+						<SamplingPeriod>1</SamplingPeriod>
+						<PidControl>
+							<Kp>100</Kp> <!-- Moderate response -->
+							<Ki>0</Ki> <!-- No integral action -->
+							<Kd>280</Kd> <!-- Light damping -->
+							<PidMode>incremental</PidMode>
+						</PidControl>
+					</CoolingDevice>
+				</TripPoint>
+			</TripPoints>
+		</ThermalZone>
+	</ThermalZones>
+	<CoolingDevices>
+		<CoolingDevice>
+			<Type>spel_controller_soc_pl1</Type>
+			<SysfsPath>/sys/class/powercap/qcom-spel:0:0/</SysfsPath>
+			<DebouncePeriod>0</DebouncePeriod>
+		</CoolingDevice>
+	</CoolingDevices>
+</Platform>
 </ThermalConfiguration>
 <!-- END -->
